###############################################################################
# BID — bidding (Dev 4)
# The whole file can be run top to bottom (request 1 passes its id to the requests after it)
#
# Covered so far: BID-001 valid bidding, BID-002 atomicity + retry,
# BID-003 realtime broadcast, BID-004 anti-sniping, BID-005 bid history
# The whole BID group is now complete
#
# ⚠️ clientRequestId must be a UUID and is "the identifier of that particular attempt"
#    - sending again with the same id + same values = retry -> you get the same bid back, not an error
#    - sending again with the same id + different values = misused id -> 409
#    For a genuinely new bid, change the trailing digits or generate a new UUID
###############################################################################

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@admin   = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@sellerA = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@buyer   = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004
@catCollectibles = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000103

# AUTH-008 — paste the tokens from `pnpm --filter api exec prisma db seed`
@adminToken   =
@sellerAToken =
@buyerToken   =

#=============================================================================
# 1. Prepare a running auction
#=============================================================================

### create a draft that has already started and not yet ended
# @name liveDraft
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bidding test item",
  "description": "Already started, not ended yet",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "USED",
  "startingPrice": 3000,
  "minBidIncrement": 100,
  "reservePrice": 4500,
  "scheduledStartAt": "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "scheduledEndAt": "2026-12-31T00:00:00.000Z",
  "imageUrls": ["https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Bidding"]
}

@liveId = {{liveDraft.response.body.$.id}}

### publish it as ACTIVE. expect 200 + status ACTIVE + biddingOpen true
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{liveId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

#=============================================================================
# 2. Accepted bids (BID-001)
#=============================================================================

### BID-001 — first bid at exactly the starting price. expect 201 + sequenceNo 1
# With no bids yet, currentPrice in the DB is 0, but the minimum is the "starting price", not 0+increment
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3000,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
}

### BID-001 — check that price and bid count moved. expect currentPrice 3000, bidCount 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}

### BID-001 — next bid at exactly +increment. expect 201 + sequenceNo 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3100,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"
}

#=============================================================================
# 3. Cases that must fail (no 500s allowed)
#=============================================================================

### amount — below the minimum. expect 400 + states the required minimum
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3150,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"
}

### amount — zero. expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 0,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000004"
}

### permissions — the seller bids on their own auction. expect 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 9000,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000005"
}

### permissions — an admin bids. expect 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 9000,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000006"
}

### permissions — not logged in. expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 9000,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000007"
}

### BID-002 — retry: same clientRequestId + same amount. expect 201 + the exact same bid
# Must return the same id/sequenceNo/placedAt, not an error
# Reason: a client retrying after a dropped connection can't tell whether a 409 means
# "duplicate because it already succeeded" or "bid rejected" — returning the original result answers clearly
# Send it as many times as you like; price and bidCount must not move
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3000,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
}

### BID-002 — check the price is unchanged. expect currentPrice 3100, bidCount 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}

### BID-002 — same clientRequestId but a different amount. expect 409
# Not a retry but a misused id — if the original bid were silently returned
# the client would think 8000 had been accepted when it never was
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 8000,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
}

### BID-002 — same clientRequestId but sent to another auction. expect 409
# Uses {{startsNowId}} from 08-auction.http (a different auction that is ACTIVE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{startsNowId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3000,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
}

### validation — clientRequestId is not a UUID. expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3200,
  "clientRequestId": "not-a-uuid"
}

### validation — auction id is not a UUID. expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/not-a-uuid/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3200,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000008"
}

### auction — an id that doesn't exist. expect 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000099ff/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3200,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000009"
}

### auction — not started yet (SCHEDULED). expect 409
# Uses {{draftId}} from 08-auction.http, published as SCHEDULED
# or create a new draft with a future scheduledStartAt and publish it
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{draftId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3200,
  "clientRequestId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a"
}

#=============================================================================
# 4. Rules that can only be proven once real bids exist
#=============================================================================

### AUC-006 — the seller edits an auction that already has bids. expect 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Someone has bid, cannot edit"
}

### AUC-006 — the seller cancels an auction that already has bids. expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Has bids, cannot cancel myself"
}

### AUC-008 — an auction with bids must rank first in the hot list
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions

#=============================================================================
# 5. Realtime broadcast (BID-003)
#=============================================================================
# .http files can't do WebSocket — this section is a manual test procedure
#
# 1) Open the browser console on any apps/web page (or use node)
#    and paste:
#
#      const s = io('http://localhost:4000/auctions', { transports: ['websocket'] });
#      s.on('connect', async () => {
#        console.log('joined', await s.emitWithAck('auction:join', { auctionId: '<liveId>' }));
#      });
#      s.on('auction:bid', (e) => console.log('auction:bid', e));
#
# 2) Send the "Accepted bids" block above again (change clientRequestId)
#
# 3) You must see the event pop up in the console immediately, looking like this:
#
#      {
#        auctionId, currency, currentPrice, reserveMet, bidCount,
#        currentEndAt, extensionCount,
#        bid: { id, amount, sequenceNo, placedAt, bidder: "S***i" }
#      }
#
# What to check:
#   - the payload must never contain reservePrice, only reserveMet (AUC-003)
#   - bidder must be a masked name only — no bidderId and no full name
#   - the label must match what GET /auctions/:id/bids returns (same mask)
#   - joining the room of an unpublished draft must return the error "Auction not found"
#   - rejected bids (400/403/409) must not emit any event
#   - a retry with the same clientRequestId must not emit the event again

#=============================================================================
# 6. Anti-sniping (BID-004)
#=============================================================================
# A bid placed with ≤ 2 minutes left pushes the end time out by another 2 minutes, at most 5 times
# and every extension is recorded in auction_extensions
#
# ⚠️ This needs an auction that is "about to end", which can't be published directly (AUC-004 won't publish
#    something already expired). Manual approach: publish normally first, then open prisma studio,
#    set current_end_at = now() + 1 minute, and then place the bid
#
# What you must see after the bid:
#   - current_end_at moved +2 minutes from its previous value (not +2 minutes from the bid time)
#   - extension_count increased to 1
#   - auction_extensions has a new row pointing to the bid just placed
#   - auction_events has EXTENDED right after BID_PLACED
#   - if a socket is left open (see block 5), you get auction:extension after
#     auction:bid, with extensionsRemaining saying how many are left

### BID-004 — bid near the end (set current_end_at close first). expect 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3200,
  "clientRequestId": "bbbbbbbb-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
}

### BID-004 — check the end time moved. Look at currentEndAt and extensionCount
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}

### BID-004 — bid again immediately. expect 201 but extensionCount must not move
# The first bid pushed the end time out 2 minutes, so this bid is already outside the window — stops a burst of bids
# from chaining extension after extension
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3300,
  "clientRequestId": "bbbbbbbb-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"
}

### BID-004 — the cap of 5
# Set extension_count = 5 and current_end_at = now() + 1 minute in prisma studio
# then send this block: the bid must succeed (201) but the end time must not move, and no new row
# is added to auction_extensions — the cap limits extensions, not bidding
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3400,
  "clientRequestId": "bbbbbbbb-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"
}

#=============================================================================
# 7. Bid history (BID-005)
#=============================================================================
# Public like the auction itself — readable without logging in
# Sending a token adds isYours, marking which rows are your own bids
#
# What to check every time:
#   - the result must never contain bidderId, only the masked bidder (S***i)
#   - the auction's seller also sees masked names, same as outsiders — no special access
#   - the same person bidding several times must get the same label on every row (so you can follow who outbid whom)
#   - ordered oldest to newest by sequenceNo

### BID-005 — a logged-out visitor reads the history. expect 200 + items ordered by sequenceNo
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids

### BID-005 — the bidder reads it. expect 200 + isYours: true only on their own bids
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### BID-005 — the seller reads it. expect 200 + names still masked
# The auction owner has no right to see who bid
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### BID-005 — 2 rows at a time. expect 200 + at most 2 items + full meta.total
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids?page=1&limit=2

### BID-005 — page 2. expect 200 + no overlap with page 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids?page=2&limit=2

### BID-005 — an auction that is still a draft. expect 404
# Even when the owner calls it — the history must not become a way to read drafts
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{incompleteId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### BID-005 — an auction that doesn't exist. expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000099ff/bids

### BID-005 — limit above the cap. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids?limit=500

### BID-005 — page is 0. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids?page=0
